" data-id=\"6ba16ec\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 0.5em 0px 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Segoe UI Historic', 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #050505; font-size: 15px;\"><div dir=\"auto\" style=\"font-family: inherit;\"><p>The Touch Sonn Foundation has donated a substantial sum of US $300,000 to CamTech University to provide loans to students at low-interest rates. This marks the first major donation from the foundation to CamTech\u2019s Endowment Fund, which was established to support student financial aid, academic programs, and infrastructure development.<\/p><p>Prof. Dr. Khieng Sothy, Founding President of CamTech University, expressed gratitude for the foundation&#8217;s support, stating that the funds received will enable the university to become more financially sustainable and increase enrollment rates, particularly among female students and those from remote areas.<\/p><p>CamTech University was established with a vision to become a leading institution in technology and science, and its mission is to provide high-quality education and promote academic excellence through innovation and entrepreneurship.<\/p><p>CamTech University welcomes all generous individuals to join this journey of shaping the future of education in Cambodia. We believe that every contribution, no matter how small, can make a significant difference in the lives of our students. Together, we can create a brighter future for our country.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-3d4b177f elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-gap-beside-yes elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-c